        <mxCell id="design-note" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontColor=#333333;fontSize=12;" value="DESIGN AND MIGRATION NOTES&#xa;10 Servers / 6 Staff PCs / 2 Admin PCs / 10 Switches. Run only the VMs required for the current task.&#xa;Port labels describe roles; actual NIC names, VMnet assignments and GNS3 runtime are not confirmed.&#xa;Document VLAN references: DMZ 110 / SERVER 120 / COMMON 150. Final mapping to retained addressing is pending.&#xa;VMnet ID is not VLAN ID. Windows VMnet1 previously used 192.168.9.1; avoid a collision with UTM1.&#xa;M1 addresses remain unchanged. M3 readdressing and the M4 192.168.150.0/24 overlap require team coordination." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1050" x="30" y="1300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="policy-note" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontColor=#333333;fontSize=12;" value="ROUTING AND VALIDATION&#xa;VyOS routes HQ subnets via 192.168.9.1. UTM1 defaults via 192.168.9.254.&#xa;Internet SNAT and internal / VPN NAT exclusions are separate policies.&#xa;VPN endpoints: UTM1 - UTM5 for office access; UTM1 - UTM4 for management.&#xa;M2 remains independent. S01: HQ staff - UTM1 - VyOS1 - classroom LAN - VyOS2 - UTM2 - SSH test server.&#xa;Preserve baseline evidence before hardening. Diagram links do not prove connectivity." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="770" x="1100" y="1300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
